## 2. Research Plan

Prioritize genes in interconnected pathways with hits: (1) TCR/BCR proximal signaling (LCP2, ITK, LAT, SLP76, CARD11 family members); (2) downstream effectors of identified kinases (AKT, MAPK pathway scaffolds and phosphatases); (3) transcription factors regulating IFNG (T-bet orthologs, EOMES partners, RUNX/CBFB complexes); (4) mTOR/TSC pathway components since TSC1 shows strong positive effect; (5) epigenetic regulators (KDM and KAT families partially screened, plus histone deacetylases). This focused approach leverages hit pathway biology to identify synergistic regulators within 128 gene capacity.

